# Needs the navigation build: flutter build apk --debug --dart-define=PROBE_AGENT=true --dart-define=PROBE_FIXTURE_WIDGETS=navigation (see the README).
# What each test shows is also in docs/compat/MATRIX.md: a matrix cell is set only from a test that ran.

before each test
  restart the app
  # Right after a restart the agent can answer while the screen is still being built (issue #793): wait for the screen's last element
  # with an id. `wait until ... appears` matches only what is on screen, so this needs a screen tall enough to show that element
  # (measured on a Pixel 6 profile); on a shorter one the wait would time out. A wait for an earlier element was not enough (measured).
  wait until #wf_open_message appears

test "the app bar's title is seen and its action is found by its tooltip"
  see "Inbox"
  see "Queries: 0"
  tap "Search"
  see "Queries: 1"
  tap #wf_search
  see "Queries: 2"

test "a pushed route is seen"
  tap "Open message"
  wait until "From: Ada" appears
  see "Message"
  see "From: Ada"

# The route rule on a device: the first route is under the opaque second one, so its title and its texts are not matched while the second is on top
# (probe_agent's finder, _isVisible and _routeOnScreen; unit test "ProbeFinder route-awareness (PT-03)").
test "the route under the top one is not seen"
  see "Inbox"
  see "Queries: 0"
  tap "Open message"
  wait until "From: Ada" appears
  don't see "Inbox"
  don't see "Queries: 0"
  don't see "Open message"

# While the pop runs (Material's page transition, about 300 ms), the leaving route is still mounted and on screen, so it is still matched: measured,
# `don't see "From: Ada"` right after `go back` and `wait until "Inbox" appears` found it. Waiting for it to go is the way to check the pop.
test "go back returns to the first route, which is seen again"
  tap "Open message"
  wait until "From: Ada" appears
  go back
  wait until "From: Ada" disappears
  see "Inbox"
  see "Queries: 0"
